Summary Risk Factors
Below is a summary of the principal risks and uncertainties we face, organized under relevant headings. These risks are discussed more fully below.
Risks related to Argentina include:
We are subject to the following risks in respect of Argentina:
•
the Argentine economy could be adversely affected by the economic, social and political measures adopted by the Argentine government;
•
the Argentine economy has experienced significant volatility in recent decades, characterized by periods of low or negative growth, high inflation, and currency devaluation;
